{"availability":"available","full":"dzid26/TeslaBatteryBLE","name":"TeslaBatteryBLE","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Kotlin","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-03T23:29:19Z","updated":"2026-10-09T23:56:25Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dzid26.github.io/TeslaBatteryBLE/","topics":[],"demo":"https://dzid26.github.io/TeslaBatteryBLE/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:04:53.870Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:04:53.870Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:04:53.870Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T06:39:52.107Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T15:04:53.870Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Your Tesla's battery, tracked locally over Bluetooth LE. No cloud, no account, nothing leaves the phone.","[]( []( [](LICENSE) -green.svg) [](docs/master-plan.md)","TeslaBatteryBLE talks to a Tesla over Bluetooth LE using an enrolled vehicle key — the same local protocol Tesla's vehicle-command uses. No Tesla account, no virtual-key cloud registration, no telemetry. Install the app, pair a key with an NFC card tap on the console, and read the car directly."],"features":["Scan & connect to nearby Teslas by advertised BLE name, with VIN-based hinting","Pair a key (CHARGINGMANAGER role by default) via Tesla's unsigned addKey flow: NFC card tap on the console + vehicle confirmation","No extra BLE channel — the car reserves one BLE channel per connected device, not per app. A dongle or keyfob always takes its own channel; the app shares your phone's link, so installed on the same phone as Tesla's…","reading is blue only while it is current (under 5 minutes old, the link up and the car awake); after that, or as soon as the link drops or the car sleeps, it turns gray and the car view, the list and the notification…","How long each state has held — the car view shows how long the car has been asleep and locked (\"